## 
An Explainable and Cross-Dataset Deep Learning Framework for Thyroid Nodule Detection and Benign–Malignant Classification

Main objectives:
1. Detect thyroid nodules from ultrasound images.
2. Classify nodules into Benign and Malignant.
3. Explain predictions using Grad-CAM.
4. Evaluate performance across different datasets.
5. Test model robustness against image quality variations.
## Research Gaps: Thyroid Nodule Detection and Classification Using Deep Learning

| No. | Research Gap                              | What You Can Work On                                                              |
| --- | ----------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| 1   | Cross-Dataset Generalization              | Train a model on one dataset and test its performance on different datasets.      |
| 2   | Explainable Artificial Intelligence (XAI) | Use Grad-CAM to explain why the model classifies a nodule as benign or malignant. |
| 3   | Class Imbalance                           | Develop techniques to handle imbalanced benign and malignant classes.             |
| 4   | Detection-Assisted Classification         | First detect thyroid nodules, then classify them as benign or malignant.          |
| 5   | Low-Quality Image Detection               | Improve model performance on blurry, noisy, and low-resolution ultrasound images. |
| 6   | Lightweight Deep Learning Models          | Develop a computationally efficient model with good classification performance.   |
| 7   | Attention-Based Detection                 | Apply attention mechanisms to improve thyroid nodule detection.                   |
| 8   | False Negative Reduction                  | Reduce the number of malignant nodules incorrectly classified as benign.          |
| 9   | Multi-Task Learning                       | Develop a single model for nodule detection, segmentation, and classification.    |
| 10  | Model Uncertainty Estimation              | Estimate prediction confidence and identify uncertain classifications.            |
| 11  | Data Augmentation Optimization            | Develop effective augmentation techniques for limited ultrasound datasets.        |
| 12  | Domain Adaptation                         | Reduce performance differences across hospitals and ultrasound imaging devices.   |

## Top 5 Recommended Research Gaps

1. Cross-Dataset Generalization
2. Detection-Assisted Classification
3. Explainable AI Using Grad-CAM
4. False Negative Reduction
5. Lightweight Deep Learning Models

Note: These are potential research gaps. You should verify their novelty through a systematic literature review before selecting your final research contribution.
